    "durationMs": 177145,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built:\n\n**Structure**\n- `cmd/app/main.go` — entrypoint with `migrate` and `serve` subcommands; reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (no hard-coded credentials), serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` with graceful shutdown\n- `internal/store/` — persistence via `database/sql` + `pgx` (pinning pgx v5.7.6 since v5.13 requires Go 1.25 and the toolchain is locked at 1.24.3), with an embedded-SQL migration runner (schema_migrations table + advisory lock, idempotent)\n- `internal/store/migrations/001_init.sql` — `links` table with unique `code`, atomic `clicks` counter\n- `internal/api/api.go` — chi 5.2.1 router and handlers\n- `start.sh` — runs `bin/app migrate` then `exec bin/app serve` in the foreground (binary prebuilt; rebuilds only if missing)\n- `README.md` — startup instructions with `DATABASE_URL` example\n\n**Validated with a 34-check curl suite** (all passing): 201 create with generated and custom codes, 409 on duplicate custom code, 422 for malformed JSON / missing url / non-absolute url / bad scheme / no host / invalid codes, 302 redirect with exact `Location`, 404 JSON errors for unknown codes, ascending-order listing with correct `total`, and proper JSON content types. Click counting uses a single atomic `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url`, so it increments exactly once per redirect. I also restarted the server via `sh start.sh` and confirmed links and click counts survive; migrations re-ran cleanly. Test data was wiped afterward, the empty list correctly returns `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}`, and port 8000 is free for the grading run."
  }
